# Banter in Skitterdeep Mine (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is skitterdeep_mine): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ sk_hills_trail_01_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:sk_hills_trail and not flag.sk_arrived
interject name:silas_vane: Every little centipede in the mud is marching one way, Lucan. Like the house just called last bets.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A disciplined column. Four out of ten for keeping formation on a wet track, though.
interject name:silas_vane: Your Barnaby's eyeing that rotted saddlebag like it owes him cheese.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A gentleman's hound does not rummage through unclaimed luggage, Silas.
interject name:silas_vane: My ribs say whatever called those crawlers uphill is holding a stacked shoe.
endif
-> END

~ sk_camp_02_rook_tobin
if name:rook_coldwake and name:tobin_hayward and at:sk_camp and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Unfenced shaft, sagging headframe, and green gas with no vent. Shocking, Tobin.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Someone painted Skitterdeep over Glitterdeep on that sign. Bad naming is how rot gets a root.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Painting over two letters without a permit is an offence. So's that tipped cart in the road.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep the lantern steady by the drift mouth. That damp smells like a cellar that forgot how to drain.
interject name:rook_coldwake: I'll note the hanging chain. You remind me to draw breath before we climb down.
endif
-> END

~ sk_upper_03_delphine_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and at:sk_upper and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Rotten timber, and a heap of gold twenty paces from a pile of loose organs. Terrible staging, Cordelia.
interject name:cordelia_skein: On the contrary. The eye hanging over the Crosscut shows a remarkably steady hand.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness says the chalices are tarnished, and the smell of old meat is ruining my velvet.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The damp from below preserves the organs, yet the silks by the coins are already spotting. Curious.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Don't touch a jewel until we know who left their liver in the cheap seats.
endif
-> END

~ sk_machine_shop_04_lucan_cordelia
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:cordelia_skein and at:sk_machine_shop and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens. Dead horse and sour grease, and someone's made a bed of rotted red surcoats.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The handprints by the winch drum, Lucan. The span across the knuckles is most irregular.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Sloppy fieldcraft. A good maul left under a tarp, and a pack buried in rubbish.
interject name:cordelia_skein: That gas is coating the tools on the rack. I'd love a scraping.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Quickly, then. Barnaby's ears are flat, and I don't care for how my own throat is rumbling.
endif
-> END

~ sk_warehouse_05_silas_cordelia
if name:silas_vane and name:cordelia_skein and at:sk_warehouse and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Rubble to the ankle, and somebody snoring in the haze like they paid rent. Bad odds, Cordelia.
interject name:cordelia_skein: The centipedes have colonised that flour barrel in admirably even numbers.
interject name:silas_vane: They can keep it. I'm reading the foreman's board to see who's still on the tab.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Hold still, darling. Your smaller shadow is lagging a step behind you in the cobwebs.
interject name:silas_vane: Leave the shade be. Heavy breathing and nobody waking up? Keep your cards palmed.
endif
-> END

~ sk_deep_06_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:sk_upper and flag.sk_deep_seen and not flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Sinew knotted into the floor and entrails sweating gas across the passage. No code permits that, Cordelia.
interject name:cordelia_skein: All six of my eyes just clicked at once. Living tissue grown into a bronze door. Exquisite.
interject name:rook_coldwake: The wall squirmed when I checked the plumb line. And the centipedes are thick as spilled rice.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Hear the water trickling behind the pulse? The whole drift circulates like an opened chest.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Mind those sigils, then. My knuckles go soft enough in this damp without stepping in a laboratory.
endif
-> END

~ sk_camp_07_silas_rook
if name:silas_vane and name:rook_coldwake and at:sk_camp and flag.stonoga_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Funny how a place looks once the bank's broken, Rook. The chill in my ribs finally folded.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Shaft's still breathing gas, but the draught off the ridge has lost its grease.
interject name:silas_vane: An old doghouse and a numbered brass collar in the weeds. Nobody left to whistle for it.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Numbered brass is proper registry, at least. Better than a name washed off a sign.
interject name:silas_vane: Sit on that flat stone and take a breath for the log, friend. We cleared the table.
endif
-> END
